S-3 negative test (SP-S3C), NEVER applied to a real build.
Flips one condition-code rule: CLHR/CLH/CLHI set C on equal operands as well as on
borrow. Applied after 0001-0004 by `make engine BUILD=build/mutant SX_EXTRA_PATCHES=...`;
tests/conformance/test_lockstep.py requires the lockstep to catch it.

--- a/Interdata/id16_cpu.c
+++ b/Interdata/id16_cpu.c
@@ -893,7 +893,7 @@
     case 0xC5:                                          /* CLHI - RS */
         rslt = (R[r1] - opnd) & DMASK16;                /* result */
         CC_GL_16 (rslt);                                /* set G,L */
-        if (R[r1] < opnd)                               /* set C if borrow */
+        if (R[r1] <= opnd)                              /* MUTANT: C on equal */
             cc = cc | CC_C;
         if (((R[r1] ^ opnd) & (~opnd ^ rslt)) & SIGN16)
             cc = cc | CC_V;
